  "question": {
    "text": "The metal which is extracted by oxidation and subsequent reduction from its ore is :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Al</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ag</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Cu</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Fe</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Cyanide process, also called Macarthur-forrest Process, method of extracting silver and gold from their ores by dissolving them in a dilute solution of sodium cyanide or potassium cyanide. The following redox reaction takes place during the extraction process.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>Ag</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><msup><mi>CN</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>[</mo><mi>Ag</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>CN</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>]</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>OH</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Ag</mi><msub><mfenced><mi>CN</mi></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>Zn</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>Ag</mi><mo>&#8595;</mo><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Zn</mi><msub><mfenced><mi>CN</mi></mfenced><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math></p>"
  }
